# Documentation

## Where things live

- [`README.md`](README.md) is the developer **entry point**: setup, run, tasks,
  Definition of Done, links into `docs/`
- [`docs/`](docs/README.md) is long-form **Studio** documentation: overview,
  architecture, features, contributing, tutorials, demos
- [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md) is the curated release history. GitHub Release
  notes for each `v*` tag come from the matching version section
- Aspected **product** docs (resolvers, HTTP API) live in the sibling
  `aspects.dev` repo (`deno task dev:docs`). Do not confuse that tree with
  `docs/`

## When you change the product

- Update the matching page under `docs/` when user-facing behavior, workflows,
  metrics, or design decisions change
- Update step-by-step tutorials under `docs/tutorials/` when button labels,
  order of steps, or expected results change
- Update README when setup, tasks, env vars, or the entry checklist change
- Add a product-facing bullet under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md` (Added /
  Changed / Fixed / Removed). Do not paste raw commit subjects
- On release, move Unreleased into a versioned section per
  [README Releasing](README.md#releasing)
- Link new major pages from `docs/README.md`
- Prefer focused pages and links over duplicating the same manual in two files

## Voice

- Direct, concrete commands and button names in tutorials
- Prefer tables where they clarify
- Early tutorials (connect, documents, search): lean steps; spare the “why”
  prose. Depth belongs on Playground Compare and Scorecard metrics (how to
  interpret numbers while optimizing indexes)
- No em dashes, en dashes, or `--` as punctuation (hyphens in flags and compound
  words are fine)

## Do not

- Do not dump Playground / Scorecard / metrics manuals back into the README
- Do not leave `docs/` stale after shipping a user-visible behavior change
- Do not leave `CHANGELOG.md` Unreleased empty after shipping user-facing work
- Keep [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) short: point at README, `docs/README.md`, and
  `.cursor/rules`
